      },
      "text": "Freshwater ecosystems support disproportionate biodiversity relative to their area but face the sharpest biodiversity declines of any ecosystem type. The three dominant threats are biological invasion, physical alteration by dams, and altered flow regimes — all of which interact with eutrophication and climate change."
    },
